NAME
       od - dump bytes in octal, hex and other formats

SYNOPSIS
       od [-A d|o|x|n] [-t TYPE]... [-abcdilosvx] [-j SKIP]
          [-N COUNT] [-w[N]] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
       Dump bytes. TYPE: a (named characters), c (characters
       and escapes), d, o, u, x followed by a size 1 2 4 8 or
       C S I L. Several types print one line each, aligned as
       GNU od aligns them. A z after a type adds the printable
       characters. f4 and f8 print floating point numbers with
       the fewest digits that read back exactly. Repeated
       lines become "*" unless -v.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

